m/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118548","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118548","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118548.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118548.patch","merged_at":"2026-04-14T12:16:32Z"},"body":"This fixes an issue that was brought to my attention by @Ivorforce and @raulsntos, where connecting to a signal on a runtime class in the Godot editor would lead to errors like:\r\n\r\n```\r\nERROR: In Object of type 'Player': Attempt to connect nonexistent signal 'hit' to callable 'Main::game_over'.\r\n   at: connect (./core/object/object.cpp:1535)\r\nERROR: In Object of type 'HUD': Attempt to connect nonexistent signal 'start_game' to callable 'Main::new_game'.\r\n   at: connect (./core/object/object.cpp:1535)\r\n```\r\n\r\nLooking at the code, we appear to (incorrectly) be making a new empty GDType for placeholders (which naturally wouldn't have any signals on it), whereas we should probably reuse the real GDType, since nothing about the type itself changes on a placeholder, just the behavior of the instance","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_